From 943eeb4d14b3d5e6cfd8489b8a60e91f0e4fc834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:37:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): the vise dialog says a setup needs its stock
 before a fit, and where the vise will land

The vise grips the stock, not the imported model. With no stock body the
dialog says so before Place, greys Fit with its reason, offers the Stock
page and shows the position rows; with a stock it says where the vise
lands and how far the jaws open (one app derivation, vise_fit, shared
with InsertVise). The three no-stock refusals lose the 'invalid
parameters:' prefix and say what to do. The browser's Stock row reads
'not set' while the stock has no body.

Fixes #1105

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
